Q_EXPORT with gcc on SunOS: q_shared.h leaves Q_EXPORT empty for gcc when
"sun" is defined (it is, by gcc on illumos and Solaris), but the CMake build
compiles everything with -fvisibility=hidden. So GetRefAPI and the modules'
vmMain/dllEntry are linked as hidden local symbols: "Can't load symbol
GetRefAPI ... can't find symbol", no renderer, and no native game modules.
gcc's visibility attribute works on SunOS: drop the !sun exception (Sun
Studio keeps its __global).

Upstream: not submitted yet; no issue or pull request about it at
https://github.com/ioquake/ioq3 (checked 2026-11-10).

--- ioq3-87a99d18206e878a20289f05ac3c16005dcae5c3/code/qcommon/q_shared.h.orig
+++ ioq3-87a99d18206e878a20289f05ac3c16005dcae5c3/code/qcommon/q_shared.h
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@
 #define Q_EXPORT __declspec(dllexport)
 #elif (defined __SUNPRO_C)
 #define Q_EXPORT __global
-#elif ((__GNUC__ >= 3) && (!__EMX__) && (!sun))
+#elif ((__GNUC__ >= 3) && (!__EMX__))
 #define Q_EXPORT __attribute__((visibility("default")))
 #else
 #define Q_EXPORT
